<title>USA: Table of Top Ten Cargo Carriers at JFK, 1996.</title>
<headline>Table of Top Ten Cargo Carriers at JFK, 1996.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Port Authority of New York and New Jersey said American Airlines headed the list of cargo carriers importing and exporting from John F. Kennedy Airport.</p>
<p>The top ten cargo airlines from New York's JFK, in order according to combined import and export tonnage handled, were;</p>
<p>1.  American Airlines</p>
<p>2.  Lufthansa Cargo</p>
<p>3.  Korean Airlines</p>
<p>4.  United Airlines</p>
<p>5.  Asiana Airlines</p>
<p>6.  DHL</p>
<p>7.  Trans World Airlines</p>
<p>8.  Polar Airlines</p>
<p>9.  British Airways</p>
<p>10. Federal Express</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
